  "Novelist and short-story writer; the author of Wide Sargasso Sea and the great novelist of the woman alone in Paris and London.",
  "Born Ella Gwendolen Rees Williams in Roseau, Dominica, on 24 August 1890; she came to England at sixteen, worked as a chorus girl and a mannequin, and published The Left Bank (1927), Quartet (1928), After Leaving Mr Mackenzie (1931), Voyage in the Dark (1934) and Good Morning, Midnight (1939). She disappeared from view and returned in 1966 with Wide Sargasso Sea. She died at Exeter on 14 May 1979.",
