  "Born Edmee Elizabeth Monica de la Pasture at Steyning, Sussex, on 9 June 1890; she worked as a nurse in the First World War and as a VAD, and published Zella Sees Herself (1917), Consequences (1919), The Diary of a Provincial Lady (1930) and its sequels, and some thirty novels. She died in Cullompton, Devon, on 2 December 1943.",
