  "Born Sylvia Nora Townsend Warner at Harpenden on 6 December 1893; she edited the ten-volume Tudor Church Music and published Lolly Willowes in 1926, followed by Mr Fortune's Maggot (1927), The True Heart (1929), Summer Will Show (1936) and After the Death of Don Juan (1938). She lived with the poet Valentine Ackland, wrote the Kingdoms of Elfin stories, and died at Maiden Newton, Dorset, on 1 May 1978.",
