  "Born Dorothy Stirrup at Blackburn, Lancashire, on 26 February 1893; she read at Liverpool University and published Young Anne (1927), High Wages (1930), They Knew Mr Knight (1934) and Someone at a Distance (1953). Her novels of the ordinary middle-class household were bestsellers of the 1930s and 1940s and were reissued to great acclaim in the 2000s. She died at Blackburn on 14 September 1966.",
